          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पैरणो (pairṇo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from paridadhāti, \"sets round; puts on clothes\". CDIAL lists Old Marwari paharaï under it (CDIAL 7835). Hindi has pahirnā; Marwadi has dropped the h."
            }
          ]
        },
